            <div xml:id="d39">

                <pb facs="0174" n="56" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg56"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">367n.1113Ganani, Samuel/6: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Jerusalem</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Knabenshue</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-09-14T14:00:00-04:00">September 14, 1929—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your August 25, 8 P.M. reported twelve American citizens killed at Hebron. Eight
                    of these are listed in your August 26, 10 P.M. and your telegram of September
                        11th<anchor n="45" xml:id="d39-f1"/> reported Samuel Genandi [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Ganani?</hi>] as having died from wounds. Urgently
                    telegraph names of any American citizens killed other than those listed in two
                    telegrams mentioned above.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
